    detection_objective: 'Write a detection rule to detect service principal privilege escalation through application administrator
      abuse by monitoring for a multi-stage attack: directory resource enumeration through API calls to identify targets,
      role definition queries to identify service principals with elevated permissions, credential addition to target applications,
      authentication as the compromised service principal using newly added credentials, and directory role assignments to
      the original account. The attack exploits the trust relationship between application administrators and their managed
      service principals, using the service principal as a privilege escalation proxy. Detection requires correlation across
      enumeration patterns, credential management, service principal authentication, and role assignment operations.'
